01:04:22.270 --> 01:04:23.530
Quick, my person, the handcuffs.

01:04:24.410 --> 01:04:25.450
Trundle him off to the who's gal.

01:04:25.510 --> 01:04:26.410
You keep out of this.

01:04:26.780 --> 01:04:28.280
But you'll look nice in bracelets, Carpenter.

01:04:28.320 --> 01:04:30.000
Why don't you get down on all fours again,

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:32.660
Waldo, it's the only time you've ever kept your mouth shut.

01:04:32.660 --> 01:04:35.650
I hope you'll forgive my wee touch of epilepsy, my dear.

01:04:35.650 --> 01:04:37.460
It's an old family custom.

01:04:37.460 --> 01:04:41.640
Well, McPherson, what does Laura's resurrection do to you?

01:04:41.640 --> 01:04:43.990
Too bad Diane Redfern can't be resurrected.

01:04:43.990 --> 01:04:47.140
I'm afraid I've interrupted what you call a pinch.

01:04:47.140 --> 01:04:49.300
Do your duty, McPherson.

01:04:49.300 --> 01:04:53.140
You know, Lidecker, you've made me change my mind.

01:04:53.140 --> 01:04:54.520
For the moment.

01:04:54.520 --> 01:04:57.330
Well, in that case, we'll have time for a little get-together.

01:04:57.330 --> 01:05:00.000
You better order us some liquor and some food, Laura.

01:05:00.440 --> 01:05:01.320
What for?

01:05:01.320 --> 01:05:04.100
People are coming to celebrate your return.

01:05:04.100 --> 01:05:06.280
Ann, and Bullitt, and Corey, everybody.

01:05:06.280 --> 01:05:07.430
Who asked them to come?

01:05:07.430 --> 01:05:09.250
I did, when I wasn't there.

01:05:09.250 --> 01:05:11.650
I phoned my man, and he's calling everyone.

01:05:11.650 --> 01:05:13.220
Why did you do that, Waldo?

01:05:13.220 --> 01:05:15.330
A sense of the fitness of things, my dear.

01:05:15.330 --> 01:05:18.690
Perhaps our friend can weave all the loose ends into a noose.

01:05:18.690 --> 01:05:19.480
Eh, McPherson?

01:05:19.480 --> 01:05:21.830
Sorry, you went to all that trouble. I've already called them.

01:05:23.940 --> 01:05:28.590
You're working yourself to death, darling.

01:05:28.590 --> 01:05:30.000
I haven't had a moment with you all.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:06:00.000
day. It's a very thirsty crowd, you know. After all, it isn't your homecoming. Aren't you being a little bit nasty, Anne? I feel nasty when I don't see you. Well, you look very sweet. That's a completely wonderful hat, darling. Now, if you'll forgive me, Laura wants a cocktail. So do I. Well, here you go. Shelby, why don't you come to your senses? You know it's all over between you and Laura. It soon will be. You haven't lost me. Why don't we get married? But, Anne, do you

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:00.660
you don't seem to

01:06:00.660 --> 01:06:01.780
realize the situation.

01:06:02.240 --> 01:06:03.100
That's why you need me.

01:06:03.440 --> 01:06:04.020
We'll get the best

01:06:04.020 --> 01:06:05.080
lawyer that money can buy.

01:06:05.700 --> 01:06:06.340
And when it's all over,

01:06:06.420 --> 01:06:06.880
we'll go away

01:06:06.880 --> 01:06:07.620
any way you wander.

01:06:08.030 --> 01:06:09.140
Forget about all this.

01:06:09.360 --> 01:06:09.940
Thanks, Anne,

01:06:09.980 --> 01:06:10.460
but you see,

01:06:10.620 --> 01:06:11.440
Laura needs me.

01:06:11.870 --> 01:06:12.230
Sorry.

01:06:20.860 --> 01:06:21.220
Thanks.

01:06:21.730 --> 01:06:22.960
If you don't mind,

01:06:23.060 --> 01:06:23.760
I'd like a word

01:06:23.760 --> 01:06:24.320
