kill Diane Redfern or anyone else then why why did you tell me the radio at your country place

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:04.080
was broken. Because it was broken. Not when I tried it. Just as I was leaving the

01:12:04.080 --> 01:12:08.310
village, I asked the local handyman to fix it. How did he get in? I always leave

01:12:08.310 --> 01:12:12.250
a key under the flower pot on the porch. You're too intelligent to make up

01:12:12.250 --> 01:12:16.960
something I could check so easily, but you're intelligent enough to have broken

01:12:16.960 --> 01:12:21.790
it yourself to strengthen your story. The main thing I want to know is why you

01:12:21.790 --> 01:12:25.360
pulled that switch on me about Carpenter. You told me last night you

01:12:25.360 --> 01:12:30.000
decided not to marry him. Yes, I guess I did. But today it's

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:39.450
was on again. Why? Well, I, I changed my mind. What are you trying to hide? Don't you realize you're

01:12:39.450 --> 01:12:44.060
involved in the murder? You've got yourself in a jam. It's not going to be easy to get out of

01:12:44.060 --> 01:12:50.290
unless you're on a level with me. There's no time for secrets. Now, did you really decide to call

01:12:50.290 --> 01:13:00.000
it off? Or did you just tell me that? Because you knew I wanted to hear it. What went on between

01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:06.650
you and Carpenter when you saw him last night? Did he persuade you to make up? Or did you

01:13:06.650 --> 01:13:12.000
agree to pretend you had? Was that it? Well, we... that is, both of us thought...

01:13:12.000 --> 01:13:16.000
He convinced you that if you broke the engagement now, people would think you believed he was

01:13:16.000 --> 01:13:20.870
guilty? Yes. But now I know it was only because he thought I was.

01:13:20.870 --> 01:13:25.480
Did you believe he was guilty? No, I'm sure he isn't. But he'd gotten himself into an awfully

01:13:25.480 --> 01:13:30.000
