01:16:39.880 --> 01:16:40.660
His very words.

01:16:41.480 --> 01:16:42.420
That doesn't mean anything.

01:16:43.520 --> 01:16:44.380
He isn't like that.

01:16:45.920 --> 01:16:47.460
Laura, you have one tragic weakness.

01:16:48.740 --> 01:16:51.280
With you, a lean, strong body is the measure of a man.

01:16:51.880 --> 01:16:52.920
And you always get hurt.

01:16:55.460 --> 01:16:57.080
No man is ever going to hurt me again.

01:16:58.310 --> 01:16:58.730
No one.

01:16:59.360 --> 01:17:00.000
Not even you.

01:17:01.180 --> 01:17:04.170
I hurt you?

01:17:04.170 --> 01:17:09.280
Laura, look at me.

01:17:09.280 --> 01:17:12.100
When a man has everything in the world that he wants,

01:17:12.100 --> 01:17:15.270
except what he wants most,

01:17:15.270 --> 01:17:17.600
he loses his self-respect.

01:17:17.600 --> 01:17:21.220
It makes him bitter, Laura.

01:17:21.220 --> 01:17:23.720
He wants to hurt someone as he's been hurt.

01:17:23.720 --> 01:17:29.570
You were a long time in finding out about Shelby,

01:17:29.570 --> 01:17:30.000
but...

01:17:31.310 --> 01:17:35.510
That's over now. We'll be back together again.

01:17:35.510 --> 01:17:40.670
Haven't you heard of science's newest triumph, the doorbell?

01:17:40.670 --> 01:17:47.730
I don't like to remind it. That was the murderer's signal.

01:17:47.730 --> 01:17:50.480
Did you eavesdrop too? I hope.

01:17:50.480 --> 01:17:54.580
I thought you'd like to know. We tested your shotgun. It isn't the one.

01:17:54.580 --> 01:17:59.860
Now that's what I call a typical move. A real key to the man's character.

01:18:00.860 --> 01:18:04.860
First he tells you that he thinks you're innocent, then proceeds to check up on you.

01:18:05.400 --> 01:18:07.400
I report that I think she's innocent.

01:18:07.520 --> 01:18:09.020
That's my own personal opinion.

01:18:09.820 --> 01:18:12.320
When I submit proof, it becomes the opinion of the department.

01:18:12.570 --> 01:18:15.070
This entire maneuver could be a trick to get you off your guard.

01:18:15.070 --> 01:18:16.670
It could be, but it isn't.

01:18:17.180 --> 01:18:18.280
I believe you, Mark.

01:18:18.880 --> 01:18:20.780
It's the same obvious pattern, Laura.

01:18:21.350 --> 01:18:26.650
If McPherson weren't muscular and handsome in a cheap sort of way, you'd see through him in a second.

01:18:27.160 --> 01:18:29.860
Waldo, I mean to be as kind about this as I know how.

01:18:30.480 --> 01:18:34.780
But I must tell you, you're the one who follows the same obvious pattern.

01:18:34.780 --> 01:18:37.770
First, it was Jacoby, then Shelby, and now I suppose...

01:18:37.770 --> 01:18:39.730
I don't think we should see each other again.

01:18:39.730 --> 01:18:42.350
You're not yourself, darling.

01:18:42.350 --> 01:18:43.320
Yes, I am.

01:18:43.320 --> 01:18:46.940
For the first time in ages, I know what I'm doing.

01:18:46.940 --> 01:18:50.550
Very well.

01:18:50.550 --> 01:18:56.840
I hope you'll never regret what promises to be a disgustingly earthy relationship.

01:18:56.840 --> 01:19:00.000
My congratulations.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:30.000
Congratulations, Macpherson. Listen to my broadcast in 15 minutes. I'm discussing great lovers of history.

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:40.990
thing I ever had to do in my whole life. All I need is the gun. What are you doing?

01:19:40.990 --> 01:19:48.980
Do you know the combination to this thing? I knew it had one. Must be somewhere.

01:20:00.120 --> 01:20:02.600
Have you ever seen this before?

01:20:02.600 --> 01:20:04.480
- No.

01:20:04.480 --> 01:20:07.310
- Waldo gave you that clock, didn't he?

01:20:07.310 --> 01:20:10.500
- Yes.

01:20:10.500 --> 01:20:14.460
